course: dictionary
lesson: 10345
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. The word transit has three meanings. «The parcel was lost in transit.» Here transit means on the way from one place to another, so the parcel went missing while it was being carried.
explain: Transit can also mean the buses, trains and subways that people use to travel. This is called public transit, and it is most often used in the US and Canada. When you read transit, look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: In science, a transit is when a planet or moon passes in front of a bigger object, such as the Sun. «Most exoplanets have been found by the transit method: a star dims slightly when a planet passes in front of it.» The clue is «passes in front of it», so transit here means passing in front.
fact: Transit means moving people or goods from one place to another.
fact: «In transit» means on the way, and not yet arrived.
fact: Public transit is the system of buses, trains and subways that people use to travel.
fact: In science, a transit is when a planet or moon passes in front of a bigger object, such as the Sun.
fact: In the transit method, a star dims slightly when a planet passes in front of it, and this helps astronomers find exoplanets.
exercise: «The parcel was lost in transit.» What does in transit mean? | Opened by the postman | Thrown away at the shop | Safely at home on the doorstep | *On its way from one place to another
exercise: In the US and Canada, what is public transit? | *Buses, trains and subways that people use to travel | A type of school bag | Planes that carry only goods | Private cars parked outside houses
exercise: In science, what is a transit? | *A planet or moon passing in front of a bigger object, such as the Sun | A star exploding in space | A planet getting bigger
test: Which phrase means on the way from one place to another? | Very old | *In transit | Fast asleep | Lost forever
test: «A star dims slightly when a planet passes in front of it.» What happens to the star? | Turns into a planet | Begins to spin faster | Grows much bigger | *Gets slightly dimmer
exam: In «a star dims slightly when a planet passes in front of it», which meaning of transit is used? | The buses and trains people use to travel | Goods carried from one place to another | A van for moving furniture | *A planet or moon passing in front of a bigger object
